<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system repurchases.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system repurchases.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system via overnight system repurchase agreements on Tuesday, a Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected the Fed to add reserves, though some had looked for a two-day, instead of an overnight, operation.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-1/2 percent, the Fed's target for the rate, at the time of the operation.</p>
<p>-- (E. Freilich, North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
